00:37:29.370 --> 00:37:31.450
from graphic design,
working with these startups?

00:37:31.450 --> 00:37:32.310
I'm just like, I love it,

00:37:32.310 --> 00:37:34.580
I love learning new things,
discovering new people.

00:37:34.580 --> 00:37:35.718
- It's also

00:37:35.718 --> 00:37:36.800
- I could have done that for 50 years.

00:37:36.800 --> 00:37:39.165
- There's also, did you
also have the feeling of

00:37:39.165 --> 00:37:41.293
there's also an amazing
part when you feel like

00:37:41.293 --> 00:37:44.330
you know something, and
a lot of other people

00:37:44.330 --> 00:37:45.727
don't know it.

00:37:45.727 --> 00:37:48.530
And then, you genuinely believe.

00:37:48.530 --> 00:37:51.330
There's an incredible
feeling of accomplishment

00:37:51.330 --> 00:37:52.940
when you know the unveil.

00:37:52.940 --> 00:37:55.963
I got ragged on so heavily
for starting a YouTube show.

00:37:55.963 --> 00:37:56.796
- Right.

00:37:56.796 --> 00:37:59.311
- Made fun of for starting a website.

00:37:59.311 --> 00:38:03.063
Got so much snarky comments
of starting an agency,

00:38:04.490 --> 00:38:09.010
writing a book, speaking,
starting a sneaker.

00:38:09.010 --> 00:38:10.630
Everything I do I get made fun of!

00:38:10.630 --> 00:38:11.463
Even now!

00:38:12.340 --> 00:38:13.390
It's a different level of people

00:38:13.390 --> 00:38:15.160
that are making fun of you.

00:38:15.160 --> 00:38:16.973
It's somebody,

00:38:18.242 --> 00:38:19.910
it's the best!

00:38:19.910 --> 00:38:21.750
It's my preference.

00:38:21.750 --> 00:38:23.660
I like the boos much more than the cheers.

00:38:23.660 --> 00:38:25.910
- That's the space I know how to navigate.

00:38:25.910 --> 00:38:27.940
That actually leads me
into my next question,

00:38:27.940 --> 00:38:29.090
if I may take another question.

00:38:29.090 --> 00:38:30.390
- Go ahead.
- Yeah.

00:38:30.390 --> 00:38:33.420
- So, I've achieved success very quickly,

00:38:33.420 --> 00:38:35.700
and it's sort of started to,

00:38:35.700 --> 00:38:37.575
I started to have some
interpersonal challenges.

00:38:37.575 --> 00:38:39.356
- Makes sense.

00:38:39.356 --> 00:38:41.204
- It's sort of interesting,

00:38:41.204 --> 00:38:43.060
and I don't really know
how to reconcile it

00:38:43.060 --> 00:38:44.660
so namely, people in my life,

00:38:44.660 --> 00:38:46.940
people who are distant and close

00:38:46.940 --> 00:38:49.720
now just treat me differently.

00:38:49.720 --> 00:38:50.850
I can give a bunch of examples

00:38:50.850 --> 00:38:51.785
- Give me some.

00:38:51.785 --> 00:38:52.760
(laughs)

00:38:52.760 --> 00:38:53.593
Just something.

00:38:53.593 --> 00:38:55.360
- Just you know, bigger hugs.

00:38:55.360 --> 00:38:57.420
My family's thrown me a
surprise birthday party

00:38:57.420 --> 00:39:00.310
when I get back from New York,

00:39:00.310 --> 00:39:01.845
which I don't want.

00:39:01.845 --> 00:39:03.480
(laughs)

00:39:03.480 --> 00:39:04.940
I found out and I shouldn't have,

00:39:04.940 --> 00:39:06.500
but like, why are you doing that?

00:39:06.500 --> 00:39:07.460
I would have never gotten a

00:39:07.460 --> 00:39:08.293
surprise birthday party

00:39:08.293 --> 00:39:09.750
if success wasn't attached to that.

00:39:09.750 --> 00:39:12.480
- So, I think that's something,

00:39:12.480 --> 00:39:15.640
the first part felt
really easy and awesome.

00:39:15.640 --> 00:39:17.400
This one I think you have
to be thoughtful about.

00:39:17.400 --> 00:39:18.293
Let me explain.

00:39:20.269 --> 00:39:23.890
There's, so I think people
are a little confused.

00:39:23.890 --> 00:39:25.610
Actually this is finally I'm excited,

00:39:25.610 --> 00:39:26.950
I think I can articulate this well.

00:39:26.950 --> 00:39:27.810
Ready?

00:39:27.810 --> 00:39:30.040
I think the boos more than the cheers.

00:39:30.040 --> 00:39:31.573
When I'm playing the game.

00:39:32.740 --> 00:39:36.040
When I'm on the ice,
when I'm on the court.

00:39:36.040 --> 00:39:36.930
Got it?

00:39:36.930 --> 00:39:38.730
That is a motivator.

00:39:38.730 --> 00:39:41.700
The second I'm off the court,

00:39:41.700 --> 00:39:42.883
it goes the other way.

00:39:44.330 --> 00:39:46.380
I think what you need to think about is

00:39:46.380 --> 00:39:49.600
reconciling what drives you professionally

00:39:49.600 --> 00:39:52.150
and not deploying that
same thing personally.

00:39:52.150 --> 00:39:54.270
- Okay, yeah that's, definitely

00:39:54.270 --> 00:39:56.400
- I'm watching, I can see it.

00:39:56.400 --> 00:39:58.500
For me, I,

00:39:58.500 --> 00:40:03.500
you're deploying cynicism
against those behaviors

00:40:03.670 --> 00:40:05.090
for no reason.

00:40:05.090 --> 00:40:06.343
There's no upside.

00:40:07.643 --> 00:40:11.840
To me, if your parents were
booing you on the court,

00:40:11.840 --> 00:40:13.960
that's a different thing
than off the court.

00:40:13.960 --> 00:40:15.050
- Right, right.

00:40:15.050 --> 00:40:15.883
- Got it?

00:40:15.883 --> 00:40:17.670
- But that also leads into

00:40:17.670 --> 00:40:18.803
just your ideas.

00:40:20.890 --> 00:40:23.990
How do you, before, when
you're not successful,

00:40:23.990 --> 00:40:25.440
you put out ideas and

00:40:25.440 --> 00:40:27.360
whether they're good or bad,

00:40:27.360 --> 00:40:28.193
even if they're good ones,

00:40:28.193 --> 00:40:30.230
you have a 50 percent chance of someone

00:40:30.230 --> 00:40:31.253
thinking that it's good or even thinking

00:40:31.253 --> 00:40:32.580
that you can execute that idea.

00:40:32.580 --> 00:40:33.738
- You know, I think

00:40:33.738 --> 00:40:34.980
- But now that you have success

00:40:34.980 --> 00:40:36.780
- Everybody thinks
everything I say is smart.

00:40:36.780 --> 00:40:37.613
- Do you find that

00:40:37.613 --> 00:40:39.960
- Here's the good news,
here's the good news.

00:40:39.960 --> 00:40:42.570
The good news is, even though I get

00:40:42.570 --> 00:40:44.790
motivated by the boos versus the cheers,

00:40:44.790 --> 00:40:46.140
that's the micro.

00:40:46.140 --> 00:40:48.183
In the macro, I can't hear anything.

00:40:49.497 --> 00:40:50.352
- Okay.

00:40:50.352 --> 00:40:52.263
- I'll explain.

00:40:53.858 --> 00:40:56.687
I just don't value anybody's opinion.

00:40:56.687 --> 00:40:59.660
And more importantly, I don't,

00:40:59.660 --> 00:41:02.300
but I don't judge them then either.

00:41:02.300 --> 00:41:04.870
If I don't value your opinion, friend,

00:41:04.870 --> 00:41:07.280
well when you say it's stupid, and I win,

00:41:07.280 --> 00:41:08.960
I don't judge you for it,

00:41:08.960 --> 00:41:11.180
because it wasn't a factor at all,

00:41:11.180 --> 00:41:13.340
so I'm not gonna impose on you either.

00:41:13.340 --> 00:41:14.810
There's a level of

00:41:14.810 --> 00:41:16.730
I think there's a sense of responsibility

00:41:16.730 --> 00:41:19.410
with success that I'd
like to put pressure on

00:41:19.410 --> 00:41:21.503
which is being the bigger person.

00:41:22.366 --> 00:41:24.760
To me, it just plays out very simply,

00:41:24.760 --> 00:41:25.870
the chess pieces.

00:41:25.870 --> 00:41:28.810
Which is like, what's in it for you

00:41:28.810 --> 00:41:30.770
to impose a negativity

00:41:30.770 --> 00:41:32.200
even though you know
they're pandering to you

00:41:32.200 --> 00:41:33.170
in a certain way.

00:41:33.170 --> 00:41:34.110
There is,

00:41:34.110 --> 00:41:34.943
you've won.

00:41:36.532 --> 00:41:38.970
To me, when I win,

00:41:38.970 --> 00:41:41.720
there is no interest in spitting on you

00:41:41.720 --> 00:41:42.823
after I beat you.

00:41:44.050 --> 00:41:45.500
- Right.

00:41:45.500 --> 00:41:47.190
Right, makes sense.

00:41:47.190 --> 00:41:48.023
- Yeah I mean,

00:41:48.023 --> 00:41:49.250
I just don't see,

00:41:49.250 --> 00:41:50.307
like, you won!

